    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d175-a2">

                <pb facs="0218" n="168" sameAs="frus:frus1894/pg168"/>

                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Treasury Department</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#small-caps">Office of
                                the Secretary</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Washington, D.
                                C.</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1894-04-19"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">April 19,
                    1894</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p rendition="#flush"><hi rendition="#small-caps">Collector of Customs</hi>, <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Astoria, Oreg.:</hi></p>
                <p>Chinese merchants domiciled in the United States, and who departed prior to
                    November 3 last, when act amending act approved May 5, 1892, entitled “An act to
                    prohibit the coming of Chinese persons into the United States” was approved, may
                        <pb facs="0219" n="169" xml:id="pg169"/> be permitted to land upon evidence
                    sufficient to satisfy you of their identity as returning merchants. Those who
                    left the United States since November last, and whose names do not appear in
                    firm name, must be excluded under opinion of Attorney-General of 6th
                    instant.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">J. G. Carlisle</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Secretary.</hi></signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Similar telegram sent to collectors of customs at the following ports:
                        Burlington, Vt., Portland, Oreg.; Port Townsend, Wash.; Suspension Bridge,
                        N. Y.; San Francisco, Cal.</p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
